      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 50-year-old male with a history of inferior myocardial infarction and stent implantation to the right coronary artery 20 days prior this admission presented with acute inferior myocardial re-infarction. Diagnostic right coronary angiography revealed a massive thrombus within the previously implanted stent. After manual aspiration through a guiding catheter, a large, fresh thrombus was removed. Subsequently, thrombolysis in myocardial infarction (TIMI) 3 flow was established, and no further intervention was required. The patient was discharged uneventfully on medical therapy."},
